  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Bionano’s optical genome mapping (OGM) and VIA software platform is gaining real commercial traction, with record first-quarter flow‑cell sales and growing utilization from the installed base. The clinical evidence base is expanding rapidly—publications in rare diseases surged 56% year‑over‑year, positioning OGM as a potential gold standard for comprehensive structural variant analysis. Adoption is broad‑based globally at leading institutions, spanning hematologic malignancies, constitutional genetics, and cell and gene therapy, suggesting OGM is moving toward standard‑of‑care status.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Under interim CEO Al Luderer, management delivered a quarterly earnings beat and top‑line results at the high end of guidance, reinforcing credibility. The strategy focuses on deepening engagement among existing users, accelerating publication of supportive data, and leveraging software alongside instrument sales. While the company remains unprofitable, commentary highlights a healthy business with positive utilization trends, indicating disciplined execution on commercial and scientific fronts without any disruptive strategic pivots.",
